  "notes": "Cash-basis county, governmental activities only (no business-type funds). Receipts/disbursements from Statement of Receipts, Disbursements and Changes in Fund Balances, Total Governmental Funds column (p4). Taxes 8,733,012 split into property 7,453,329, motor vehicle 812,887 and lodging 466,796 using the Statement of Activities (p2); these sum exactly to the Taxes line. Local 2,039,574 split into charges for services 1,306,014, interest 605,590 and miscellaneous 127,970 (p2, ties exactly). Intergovernmental kept as one line (state vs federal not broken out). Beginning cash = beginning fund balances 13,611,774 and ending 11,940,366 (p4); roll-forward ties. Transfers in and out both 2,667,522, net zero. Balance sheet is the Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis (p1): cash 6,027,112 there vs 6,022,154 on governmental funds statement p3 (as printed; total assets agree at 11,940,366). Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p14) covers the General Fund column of the combining statement; the sub-funds (Reappraisal Sinking, Inheritance Tax, County Medical Relief, State Institutions, Veteran's Aid) come from the combining pages (p5-6) so there is no double counting. Road and ARP funds from budget schedules (p15-16; Road disbursements one line only). Nonmajor funds have more than 6 columns, so the Total Nonmajor Funds column (p13) is used; the nonmajor combining pages p7-p13 were read. General Fund detail 'Local' lines categorised as charges for services by the Statement of Activities mix (review). Read pages 1-16 of 16.",
  "report_discrepancies": [
    {
      "check": "balance_sheet",
      "difference": 4958,
      "source_page": 1,
      "note": "Statement of Net Position (p1) prints Cash 6,027,112 and Restricted cash and investments 3,961,643; governmental funds statement (p3) prints Cash 6,022,154 and Restricted cash 3,346,044 + restricted investments 620,557 = 3,966,601. The two statements classify 4,958 (Adult diversion) differently; total assets agree at 11,940,366. Figures kept as printed on p1."
    }
  ]
